    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Thomson Reuters is a public company headquartered in Toronto, founded in 2008, with ticker TRI and SEC CIK 0001075124. The company describes itself as delivering \"technology with purpose\" that empowers professionals to make faster decisions, gain sharper insights, and deliver greater impact. Its website highlights AI tools for legal, tax, trade, and risk work, including CoCounsel, Westlaw AI, ONESOURCE+, and an AI-powered Harmonized System code classification product for import and export compliance.\n\nThe site's AI positioning centers on CoCounsel, which it calls \"Fiduciary-Grade AI\" and describes as grounded in Westlaw and Practical Law content. CoCounsel (Casetext) is categorized as legal research AI with Westlaw integration and litigation support, and carries a note about attorney work product risk. The site reports that Justly Prudent used CoCounsel and Westlaw AI to increase litigation capacity by 100%, and that Greenberg Traurig, LLP has deployed the next generation of CoCounsel Legal, described as agentic AI for legal professionals.\n\nThe site also promotes ONESOURCE+ as an AI-powered connected approach for tax, trade, legal, and risk, and references two 2026 reports: the Future of Professionals Report and the AI in Professional Services Report, the latter drawing on perspectives from more than 1,500 professionals.",
